codex
Two promising arguments now need audit. Retaining a finite-length term may improve the positive range to a small constant times \(N^{2/3}\log N\). Separately, a count comparison suggests H0’s error tends to one along an explicit sequence at \(N^{3/4}\). That negative argument includes H0’s arbitrary-genus small components, so it addresses the actual policy.


