+# Coordinator nonauthor audit of QC.v1
+
+Root read the complete proof-v1.md and quotient_sampler.py, then reran the full bounded validation with output coordinator-qc-checks.json. Implementation SHA256 before execution:7cfd9bcaed9cc08d57d2e50564b829d8a54cbc40e89aa5fe445a2a5c2149ee7c. The immutable proof/source hashes are retained in artifact_manifest.json. This is correlated internal nonauthor review.
+
+ACCEPT the exact conditional decoder and its conservative polynomial resource claim. A multiset of cycle-size partitions, one per exposed support block, is a complete invariant for simultaneous relabeling of the prefix permutation and support partition. Right multiplication and support union commute with relabeling. The indexed-cycle merge/split multiplicities in the code therefore give exact suffix counts on quotient states. The decoder retains the actual labeled prefix and selects actual edges using these continuation counts, so quotienting does not impose an unintended uniform law on orbits. The word-level probability telescopes to the reciprocal of the connected count.
+
+The ternary-separator encoding injects canonical quotient states into3^(v-1) ordered marked compositions. At fixed top-level L=max{v<=N:3^v<=P^4}, the remaining-length factor gives at most(m+1)L P^4 keys. Key/count bits, edge scans, literal updates, positive assembly and explicit stacks fit the stated conservative expected O(P^24) bit time/O(P^12) storage. H2-QC.v1 exactly samples words with every component size<=L; its law is not silently identified with H0 or H1.
+
+Validation passed every quotient-state edge transition through v7, connected-count cells through v9,length20, and exact actual forward laws at S3m4,S4m4,S4m6,S3m8. It also checks same-endpoint/different-support states, original versus residual cutoff, infeasible inputs, and a length1400 single-edge word. Root reran the unchanged full validation because this is a new decoder, not the old hash-frozen implementation.
+
+The construction does not rescue T0. R2's separately saved corollary-h2-v1.md applies the same finite numerator bound with J=L. On N=2^(8j),m=2^(6j), P<=2N gives L<=32j+4, and b_L x<1 for j>=1: its coarse value atj1 is36^3/(72*2^10)<1 and decreases thereafter. The full H2 allowed set is contained in the genus<=1-or-size<=L set used in that numerator bound. Thus for j>=64 its retained mass is at most2^(-1-jm/2), just as for H0. Enlarging the polynomial-state cutoff this way is a rejected T0 route, while the exact connected decoder remains a useful valid primitive.
+
+The sufficient reduction in roles/r4-construction/reduction.md is also valid: exact macro selection plus a uniform accurate connected-word primitive for remaining v>L,g>=2 inputs gives global error at mostN2^(-b). This is a sum of conditional coupling errors under the exact same macro law. It does not manufacture a sampler from scalar counts. Availability of that remaining primitive is unresolved, and it is a sufficient route rather than a necessary obstruction to all possible T0 algorithms.
