+Validation passed every quotient-state edge transition through v7, connected-count cells through v9,length20, and exact actual forward laws at S3m4,S4m4,S4m6,S3m8. It also checks same-endpoint/different-support states, original versus residual cutoff, infeasible inputs, and a length1400 single-edge word. Root reran the unchanged full validation because this is a new decoder, not the old hash-frozen implementation.
+
+The construction does not rescue T0. R2's separately saved corollary-h2-v1.md applies the same finite numerator bound with J=L. On N=2^(8j),m=2^(6j), P<=2N gives L<=32j+4, and b_L x<1 for j>=1: its coarse value atj1 is36^3/(72*2^10)<1 and decreases thereafter. The full H2 allowed set is contained in the genus<=1-or-size<=L set used in that numerator bound. Thus for j>=64 its retained mass is at most2^(-1-jm/2), just as for H0. Enlarging the polynomial-state cutoff this way is a rejected T0 route, while the exact connected decoder remains a useful valid primitive.
+
+The sufficient reduction in roles/r4-construction/reduction.md is also valid: exact macro selection plus a uniform accurate connected-word primitive for remaining v>L,g>=2 inputs gives global error at mostN2^(-b). This is a sum of conditional coupling errors under the exact same macro law. It does not manufacture a sampler from scalar counts. Availability of that remaining primitive is unresolved, and it is a sufficient route rather than a necessary obstruction to all possible T0 algorithms.
